WEBVTT

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:03.580
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.950
Start it off with a Doki! It's Shugo Chara time!

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:08.690
Easter's finally started putting its ultimate plan into action!

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:12.490
And signs are pointin' to a certain character coming back! It's gonna be wild!

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:15.790
Let's find Ikuto-san so we can save him!

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:18.140
Totally! You can do it, Amu-chan!

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:19.470
Don't give up, Amu-chan!

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.720
Go, go, Amu-chan! Desu!

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.710
We'll be right there with you!

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:24.770
Doki!

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:43.180
If you were to walk so the wind fluttered the edge of your cape,

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:49.570
people would look up at you in quiet admiration.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:56.870
You can say spicy things like "it's not my style," if you want,

00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:03.290
but I know who you really are because I'm your friend!

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:05.160
Stand! Bow!

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.690
Nice and orderly now!

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:10.530
And once that's done,

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:15.800
it's time to start the school day.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:23.420
I like Mondays because I can see all my friends.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:29.820
There's nothing wrong with being abnormally happy.

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:36.990
At lunch break, we have tea in the Royal Garden,

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:44.330
where I tell you all my secrets!

00:01:56.870 --> 00:02:02.800
Right now, you are all trying to intercept a large meteor and change its orbit.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:09.690
I've arranged for someone to be at the school gates who may be of assistance.

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:11.630
And one more thing.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.990
That picture book...

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:18.950
Libra's lucky item for this month is a picture book.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:21.740
Now everything's set.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:23.690
Thank you, Tsukasa-san!

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:28.490
And why am I doing this exactly?

00:02:28.490 --> 00:02:31.110
So the person Tsukasa-san said could help...

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:32.880
...was Nikaidou-sensei.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.860
Man, that pesky Chairman and his bothersome requests...

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.720
They're not bothersome!

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:42.100
<i>You're</i> the one who told us not to worry about Ikuto.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.920
Here is the proof-dechu.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:50.730
And I'm not so sure he's in as much 
trouble as you think he is.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:54.860
Sure didn't turn out the way he said, did it?

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:57.690
Ikuto!

00:02:58.180 --> 00:02:59.860
You lied.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:02.230
And you call yourself a teacher.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.690
Fine, be that way!

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:05.910
I'll help you out!

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.230
Of course you will.

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:08.540
Got that right!

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.830
Thanks, Sensei!

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:15.790
Episode 98
Reborn! My Radiant Dancing Princess!

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:24.010
The incredibly tight hold they have on Ikuto is alarming.

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:28.310
Easter's plan must be reaching the final stages.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:29.590
That's quite possible.

00:03:29.590 --> 00:03:31.920
So what should we do?

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:35.610
Let's check out a safe house for the science team I know of.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.780
There might be...

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:41.390
...some clue.

00:03:41.390 --> 00:03:42.280
Um...

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:43.900
What's the matter?

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.340
We can't fight on empty stomachs.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:47.610
Niboshi!

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:49.830
First we fuel up!

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:51.040
Yup-dechu!

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.870
These are pretty good.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:54.550
Yeah, they are.

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:58.280
Don't just go all "snack time" on me!

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.780
And why not? What's it to you?

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:02.070
Because! You'll get food all over my car!

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.170
S-Sensei, the light!

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:17.190
Sensei, I will clean up afterwards, so just relax and drive.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.840
Would you like some minty gum?

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:22.770
It'll Su-weep those icky feelings all away!

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:24.310
It's okay. I'm good.

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:25.410
Say, "Ah!"

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:26.410
But I said...

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:27.910
"Ah!"

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:30.990
Su's really good at handling Sensei.

00:04:30.990 --> 00:04:32.870
You know what they say about hostages and their captors...

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:33.800
Here!

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.550
Nothing's here.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:49.540
Although, I can tell that someone used this place recently.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:54.920
The power's still on.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:56.150
Sensei?

00:04:56.450 --> 00:04:59.040
It'd be nice if we could find something here...

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:01.820
Yukari?

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:03.400
It's Sanjo-san!

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.530
It says to enter a PIN number.

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:08.730
Tsukumo, huh?

00:05:08.730 --> 00:05:11.450
If that guy were to choose a PIN...

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:17.630
Amazing, Sensei!

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:18.710
How'd you know?

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:21.310
It's Yukari's birthday.

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.230
Why would he choose her birthday?

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:26.540
I'll just ignore that question.

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:31.750
Those Easter guys sure are concocting something diabolical.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.750
A radio broadcast?

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:40.100
Those are formulas for making a radio broadcast of a special type of sound wave.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:43.860
I bet they want to send Ikuto-kun's music over the radio.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:46.450
So Ikuto will have to perform again?

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:50.700
Over the radio, the rate of X Egg extraction would be lower,

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:54.320
but it will be heard by a larger audience over a greater area.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.250
At this rate...

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:00.330
Ikuto's heart will just keep getting hurt-nya.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:04.100
I can imagine how you feel, Yoru.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:08.640
To be so powerless when your bearer is in trouble...

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:10.720
That'd make even <i>me</i> cry...

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:14.840
Don't worry there, Yoru-tan!

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.060
We'll save 'im, promise!

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:18.600
Yeah, Yoru!

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:20.890
We'll do it. Just wait and see!

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:22.630
So...

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:24.550
You can do it, Yoru!

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:26.210
Keep on fighting, Yoru!

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:28.110
You can do it, Yoru!

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:29.950
Keep on fighting, Yoru!

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.760
You can do it, Yoru!

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.920
Keep on fighting, Yoru!

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:34.660
Those guys make a big deal outta everything-nya.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:43.210
Temari...

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:43.900
Huh?

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:45.800
Don't mind me.

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:50.910
Sensei, now what?

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.810
I've decided where we should head next.

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:53.300
Where?

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.070
Before I tell you...

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:57.990
Maybe you should call your parents.

00:06:57.990 --> 00:06:59.640
It's getting late, you know.

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:05.100
They said it's okay as long as I'm with you.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:08.570
So did mine, Nikaidou-sensei.

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:10.530
For some reason, people seem to trust you.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.690
Sensei's a hit with all the moms, isn't he?

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:14.370
You think?

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:18.020
You always look so scruffy people assume you don't have a girlfriend.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:20.280
I guess you naturally trigger their maternal instincts.

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:22.140
That's quite enough of that!

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:24.500
Hurry up and call your parents, Hinamori-san!

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:32.470
I just wish... you hadn't kept secrets from us...

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.930
I can't tell her the truth.

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:40.530
But that means I'll be lying to them again...

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:46.510
Some work for the Guardians?

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:47.270
Yeah...

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:49.920
Sure.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:51.060
Really?

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:52.810
Just be careful.

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:55.410
And don't give your teacher any trouble.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:56.950
I-I won't...

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:59.240
It's important, right?

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:02.460
You can tell us all about it when you get home.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:07.000
We trust you, Amu.

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:11.640
Thanks...

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:22.940
And this is...

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:24.390
FM Inter.

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:27.320
One of Easter's affiliated companies.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:30.880
If they were planning on doing a radio broadcast, it'd have to happen here.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:33.210
All righty! Let's bust in!

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:36.740
Excuse me, I have a question...

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:38.710
He's asking normally.

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:43.260
So there's no broadcast like that on their schedule?

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:48.410
Right. She said this station doesn't do live broadcasts.

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:53.310
But it's part of Easter! They could play it off the schedule!

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:56.550
Oh, hey, it's you!

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:00.830
I'm back for more!

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:02.270
Just like last time...

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:03.740
I am...

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:06.560
the charismatic fortune-teller who just happens to be passing by...

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:08.980
Saeki Nobuko!

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:10.560
She's back!

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:13.240
Thanks for your courtesy.

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:15.020
Amu-chi! Amu-chi!

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:21.150
Nobuko-chi's fortune-telling helped you find me and Rima-tan when we were lost, right?

00:09:22.280 --> 00:09:24.540
That's true, yeah...

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.520
Are you suggesting we use her fortune-telling?

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:30.200
You want to save someone, don't you?

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:32.050
Someone important to you.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:36.020
See, see?

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:39.260
All right, I'll do a special reading for you.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:40.820
Are you sure?

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:42.040
Yes.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:45.080
Louis Antoine-sama also says that Capricorns should

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:49.080
"take special care during unexpected second meetings."

00:09:49.080 --> 00:09:49.880
Who is that?

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:51.510
What? Haven't you heard of him?

00:09:51.510 --> 00:09:53.600
Louis Antoine Tsukasa.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:57.650
He's this new, gorgeous, pretty boy fortune-teller!

00:09:57.650 --> 00:09:59.970
Tsukasa-san, what are you doing?

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:03.330
It says that Libra's lucky item is a picture book...

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:07.620
Madame, we're looking for this little guy's bearer.

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:13.110
White tower.

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:14.420
Violin.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.880
An amusement park? Maybe not...

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:19.890
But somewhere with a lot of open space.

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:23.500
An amusement park with a white tower?

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:25.800
Does such a place exist?

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:28.480
Amu-chan, Amu-chan, look at that!

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:32.520
It's right under our noses!

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:35.260
In fact, it was so big we totally missed it.

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:38.320
"A theme park for growing kid's dreams?"

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:42.540
"Dream Egg Land, Opening Soon."

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:43.980
Easter!

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:45.700
What's "Dream Egg" in Japanese?

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.890
"Yume no tamago."

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:49.290
Easter, you fiends!

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:53.400
How dare they do this after yanking out so many X Eggs!

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:55.090
Indeed, it's unforgivable!

00:10:56.190 --> 00:11:00.510
Oh yes, I heard they're holding a concert to celebrate the grand opening.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:02.980
A violin concert, if I recall correctly.

00:11:02.980 --> 00:11:03.910
Amu-chan.

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:04.880
Yeah.

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:07.440
Thanks, Madame Nobuko!

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:12.170
I don't know what you're up to, but you'd better hurry!

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:14.530
The clock is ticking!

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:17.170
Why is she saying it to the camera?

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:18.610
Hey, over here!

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:36.720
Once we start the broadcast, the Guardians are sure to come running.

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:39.670
Though they won't know that's part of our plan.

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:44.230
Your job is far from over.

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.770
Sensei, get a move on!

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:50.210
Not over the speed limit, no way.

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:57.270
Tadase, when does the broadcast start?

00:11:57.610 --> 00:12:00.200
It says tonight, at 7 o'clock.

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:01.680
7 o'clock?

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:03.220
It's almost time.

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:04.410
Sensei!

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:07.950
And that's all for today's broadcast!

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:11.410
Keep your dial tuned to FM Inter!

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:17.300
The violin's X Egg energy is stable.

00:12:17.300 --> 00:12:19.680
The Embryo Catcher is set to go.

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:20.670
Okay!

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:24.470
Ten seconds until broadcast!

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:33.230
9, 8, 7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1!

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:44.280
Dream Egg Land
Grand Opening

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:45.530
Ikuto!

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:14.450
Look at that!

00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:17.980
The sky is full of X Eggs!

00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:20.570
I've got a bad feeling about this...

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:24.950
Look, everyone, over there.

00:13:30.940 --> 00:13:33.400
Ikuto, just hang on.

00:13:33.400 --> 00:13:34.750
We're coming for you!

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:41.680
The stars foretell...

00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:44.090
No, enough of this.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:50.020
Those children might be able to alter the stars' paths.

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:53.060
It's all in your hands.

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:05.510
What's the problem?

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:09.400
We must allow him a moment's rest.

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:12.660
If we continue, Ikuto-kun will...

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:16.340
Collect more X Eggs!

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:23.000
That's my only concern.

00:14:30.560 --> 00:14:33.350
Looks like the broadcast is coming from that tower.

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:36.210
That's probably where Ikuto-kun is.

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:40.150
Hey, wait! You guys!

00:14:40.450 --> 00:14:42.360
Ikuto, we're coming for you-nya!

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:47.700
Sheesh...

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:51.570
It shut!

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:58.120
The Guardians have broken in!

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:01.710
Faster than I expected.

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:06.130
We still do not have enough X Eggs.

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:10.130
This is the first song to herald the opening of Dream Egg Land.

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:13.870
I will ensure that everyone enjoys it to the last note.

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:19.920
Wait, guys!

00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:21.200
Wait for Rima-tan!

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:25.310
Rima!

00:15:25.830 --> 00:15:27.370
Fujisaki-kun!

00:15:27.370 --> 00:15:29.150
Go on ahead without me!

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:31.170
Amu-chan, let's hurry!

00:15:31.170 --> 00:15:33.010
Thanks, Nagihiko!

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:38.800
They're too fast...

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:39.960
Rima...

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.290
Rima-chan!

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:43.250
Nagihiko.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:45.050
Are you okay?

00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:46.040
Come on.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:48.750
I won't hold hands with a liar.

00:15:49.230 --> 00:15:50.910
What are you talking about?

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:54.070
I overheard your conversation before.

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:56.440
Nobuko-chi, thanks!

00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:58.410
So then, if you'll excuse us.

00:15:58.410 --> 00:15:59.980
Wait a moment.

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:05.590
You were a girl the last time we met, weren't you?

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:11.740
You might have fooled me then, but I can sense that you have the same guardian spirits.

00:16:11.740 --> 00:16:14.870
The same as that pony-tailed girl.

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:19.580
Nagihiko, is it true?

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:24.670
Oh dear, this is a problem.

00:16:27.970 --> 00:16:32.170
Think you could keep this a secret from the others for a little while?

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:35.100
What do you think, Kusukusu?

00:16:35.100 --> 00:16:38.680
What should we do? What should we do?!

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:38.680
Pretty please?

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:45.190
It's the X Eggs that were gathered by the violin!

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:50.610
Amu-chan!

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:53.440
Tightrope Dancer!

00:16:58.410 --> 00:16:59.700
Rima?

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.740
I'll handle this.

00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:03.210
Get going while you have the chance!

00:17:03.210 --> 00:17:04.150
But...

00:17:04.150 --> 00:17:05.210
Don't worry!

00:17:07.700 --> 00:17:09.300
I'll stay here, too!

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:11.830
Can't leave a girl all by herself, after all.

00:17:11.830 --> 00:17:13.520
Nagihiko...

00:17:13.520 --> 00:17:16.160
Ikuto's waiting, Amu.

00:17:16.160 --> 00:17:18.760
Get going! Believe in us!

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:22.980
Right! Thanks, guys!

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:24.700
We'll be waiting for you.

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:25.810
So come back to us, okay?

00:17:28.090 --> 00:17:29.050
Wait!

00:17:30.460 --> 00:17:32.820
Your opponents are over here!

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:38.160
Will Rima-tan and Nagi be okay?

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:41.240
Right now, all we can do is believe in them and press on!

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:42.720
Believe...

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:44.590
Believe in your friends...

00:17:44.590 --> 00:17:46.250
Believe in your family...

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:50.180
It feels great to believe in others...

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:55.770
And because so many people believe in me, I won't hesitate anymore!

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:59.830
I would've been fine by myself.

00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:02.590
Now, don't say that.

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:04.430
We share a special secret, right?

00:18:10.090 --> 00:18:11.360
What speed!

00:18:19.590 --> 00:18:22.490
That violin's made them even stronger!

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.330
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:28.350
I'm no good at running, so it's...

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:29.570
...impossible.

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:30.960
Studying is just...

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:32.040
...impossible.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:33.340
That's...

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:36.490
It's the voices of the children whose hearts' eggs have been X'ed!

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:37.790
I'm clumsy, so it's...

00:18:37.790 --> 00:18:38.940
...impossible.

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:40.340
I'm no good at arithmetic...

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:41.560
...impossible.

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:43.390
I can't speak English...

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:44.850
For me it's just...

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:46.100
For me it's just...

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:51.400
I know how just they feel.

00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:59.360
What a shame.

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:03.240
Why do you play female roles when you're a boy?

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:06.420
Your dancing is quite captivating,

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:10.210
but don't you think it would be far more refined if you actually were a woman?

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:17.110
I agree, I could never compare to a real girl.

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:21.100
From now on, I'll be maturing as a man more and more.

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:24.520
I won't be able to keep dancing like I do now.

00:19:25.950 --> 00:19:28.650
Like a real girl...

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:32.020
How worthless.

00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:34.380
Why do you keep saying things are impossible?

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:37.070
You just decided that to make yourself feel better!

00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:42.610
Sure, there are things you can't do, things that seem impossible,

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:45.270
but that's what makes everybody unique!

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:52.210
Whether it's comedy, sports, or anything...

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:56.940
Just do the best you can to refine your art and technique!

00:19:56.940 --> 00:19:58.640
What she said!

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:03.340
So I was making excuses?

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:06.580
I'll get the X Eggs' attention.

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:08.800
Take that opportunity to attack.

00:20:08.800 --> 00:20:09.800
But...

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:10.930
I'll be fine.

00:20:13.890 --> 00:20:16.860
Blaze Shoot!

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:29.970
That's right! That's it!

00:20:29.970 --> 00:20:33.260
"It's impossible for a boy like me to dance like a girl."

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:35.540
That was just an excuse!

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:39.200
I've been running away.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:43.260
From the fact that I wasn't able to dance like a girl.

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:45.090
But...

00:20:45.980 --> 00:20:49.010
There's no reason to act like a girl!

00:20:49.740 --> 00:20:52.900
The dance that only I can do...

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:57.730
The dance that only I, a boy raised as a girl, can do...

00:21:02.260 --> 00:21:04.020
I'm sure it's out there!

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:20.090
Temari...

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:28.330
Temari!

00:21:35.070 --> 00:21:37.670
It's been too long, Nagihiko.

00:21:37.670 --> 00:21:41.040
I guess you found what you've been looking for.

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:42.420
Yes!

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:45.510
Sorry it took me so long, Temari.

00:21:46.150 --> 00:21:48.820
Temari, I'm subbing out!

00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:50.530
As you wish.

00:21:51.820 --> 00:21:54.460
My heart: Unlock!

00:21:58.010 --> 00:21:59.500
Amazing...

00:22:13.090 --> 00:22:15.970
Character Transformation: Yamato Maihime!

00:22:27.870 --> 00:22:33.220
You sure do seem determined.

00:22:34.630 --> 00:22:39.270
So even if you screw up, it'll somehow turn out all right.

00:22:39.970 --> 00:22:46.640
How about you just trust in yourself?

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:53.100
Take that first step and everything will work out fine.

00:22:53.710 --> 00:23:00.030
Even if people see through your cool exterior, keep marching on.

00:23:00.450 --> 00:23:09.110
Look up at the blue sky and everything will reset!

00:23:09.690 --> 00:23:12.750
Take it easy! Take it easy!

00:23:13.030 --> 00:23:23.290
Try to relax those shoulders and clear your mind.

00:23:23.290 --> 00:23:30.000
The more you do it, the easier it'll get, so keep taking it easy.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:35.200
Ride the flow of time and you'll be...

00:23:36.260 --> 00:23:39.000
Shining! Shining! Shining!

00:23:50.410 --> 00:23:55.410
Theme parks should be fun, but all we've had is trouble!

00:23:55.410 --> 00:23:58.040
I'll do my best to save Ikuto!

00:23:58.040 --> 00:24:00.960
I'm sure it'll be fine if we all work together!

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:03.750
We Guardian Characters will do our best as well!

00:24:03.750 --> 00:24:05.990
But will I even get a turn?

00:24:05.990 --> 00:24:08.830
Is that what concerns you most?

00:24:09.980 --> 00:24:12.160
Next time on Shugo Chara!! Doki:

00:24:12.160 --> 00:24:14.600
Our Feelings, United! The Guardians' Battle!

00:24:14.600 --> 00:24:15.940
Him, and her, too...

00:24:15.940 --> 00:24:17.510
Everyone's gonna help out!

00:24:17.730 --> 00:24:19.720
Wait for us, Ikuto!
